## Navigation

Tool priority — use the first available:

1. **Symbol-aware index** (e.g. jcodemunch / sourcegraph / language server)
   — surgical lookup without full-file reads. Index once after clone, refresh
   after large commits.
2. **Knowledge graph** (e.g. graphify) — targeted node queries for
   cross-file dependency lookups; query the JSON, don't read the whole report.
3. **`ANATOMY.md` + `docs/wiki/`** — broad orientation on an unfamiliar area.
   Read once per session, not once per task. Regenerated by `/anatomy`.
4. **Direct Read + grep** — fall back when no tools are available.

## Project memory

`.claude/memory/MEMORY.md` is the team-shared, committed-to-git memory layer
for this repo. Writes are governed by the `project-memory` skill at
`.claude/skills/project-memory/SKILL.md`. Use `/remember <fact>` to save
explicitly. Personal preferences (style, role, tooling taste) route to
user-level memory at `~/.claude/projects/.../memory/` instead.

The skill MUST refuse to save anything already covered by this file,
`.claude/rules/`, `ANATOMY.md`, `docs/wiki/`, or `git log` — memory is for
facts not derivable from code, conventions, or history.

## /cc-audit

Audits this repo's `.claude/` config against a strict-by-default profile,
fans out per-area sub-skills in parallel, and emits a plan-mode diff
bundle. Run `/cc-audit` (plan-only), `/cc-audit --dry-run` (diff, no
writes), or `/cc-audit --apply` (scaffold with per-cluster confirmation).

